  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\nAn upper ridge remains entrenched over the southern and \nsoutheastern CONUS this weekend, resulting in a zonal mean \nsynoptic flow across the Great Lakes and upper Ohio Valley \nregions through at least early next week. This will support \ncontinued active weather for the local area as periodic \nshortwave activity developing upstream tracks eastward across \nthe region. Machine-learning convective hazard guidance \ncontinues to indicate some potential for periods of heavy rain \nand/or severe weather as long as this pattern remains in place,\nwhich will need to be monitored. Global ensembles then favor a\npattern shift late next week with broad upper troughing setting\nup over eastern Canada (and upper ridging out west). If that \nends up verifying, it could point towards a period of drier \nweather on the horizon under northwest flow.",
